  "name": "Immunoglobulin G (IgG) ",
  "code": "IgG",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>IgG Test Result</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>IgG Antibodies Positive</div></td><td><div>A positive result for IgG antibodies indicates past exposure to the specific pathogen or antigen. It suggests that the individual's immune system has encountered the pathogen before and has produced IgG antibodies to provide long-term immunity. IgG antibodies remain in the body even after the infection has resolved.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>IgG Antibodies Negative</div></td><td><div>A negative result for IgG antibodies indicates no past exposure to the specific pathogen or antigen. It suggests that the individual's immune system has not encountered the pathogen before, and there is no existing immunity to that particular pathogen.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Indeterminate</div></td><td><div>In some cases, the IgG test results may be inconclusive or borderline. Additional testing or clinical evaluation may be required to determine the significance of the results.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
